include "../../linux.mereo"

-- REJECTED on purpose: the write side of the same decidable check.
--
-- Worse than the read: a store past a known backing corrupts whatever the frame
-- laid out next to it, which is generally another live slot. The read and the
-- write go through the same function, so this pins that the store path reaches
-- it -- it did not at first, the check having been added where VALUES are
-- resolved and a store's address never passing through there.
--
--   refused:  writes 101 bytes into 'block', which is 8 bytes

program goes
  block is 8 bytes

  [block + 100 : 1] is 7

  ensure [block + 0 : 1] == 0
end
